\subsection{Key terms}

\begin{tabular}{@{}p{3.6cm}p{10.4cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Term} & \textbf{Meaning} \\
\midrule
Binary counter & Sequential circuit that advances its binary output by one on each active clock transition. \\
Ripple‑carry counter & Counter where the clock of each flip‑flop is driven by the output of the previous stage, causing a propagation delay that ``ripples'' through the bits. \\
Synchronous counter & Counter in which all flip‑flops share a common clock and toggle conditions are generated combinationally, eliminating ripple delay. \\
Shift register & Linear array of flip‑flops that moves stored bits left or right on each clock pulse. \\
Serial‑in parallel‑out (SIPO) & Shift register type where data enters one bit at a time and the whole word becomes available on parallel outputs after $n$ clocks. \\
Parallel‑in serial‑out (PISO) & Shift register type where a full word is loaded simultaneously and then shifted out serially. \\
Ring counter & A shift register with a single `1' that circulates continuously, used for sequencing and pulse generation. \\
Timing diagram & Graphical plot of signal levels versus time, used to verify the temporal behavior of sequential circuits. \\
Propagation delay & The time taken for a change at the input of a flip‑flop or gate to appear at its output; critical in ripple designs. \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
